{"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The lexicographically first minimum colouring of the simple graph: on each connected","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"component, of all its colourings with its own chromatic number of colours, the one whose","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"colour vector (in ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order) is lexicographically least, Khuller and Vazirani’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"lexicographically first k-colouring (1991) with k = the component’s χ. So within a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"component colours appear in order of first use, colour classes are numbered by their least","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertex, a bipartite component is coloured by its ","type":"text"},{"code":"bipartition()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" sides (left 0), and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"colorCount == chromaticNumber()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Components are not coupled: a bipartite one keeps two","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"colours beside a triangle.","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Instance Method","symbolKind":"method","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"lexicographicallyFirstMinimumColoring"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14ColoringModule0A0V","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Coloring"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/ColoringModule\/ExactColoring.swift#L659","fileName":"ExactColoring.swift"},"extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","title":"lexicographicallyFirstMinimumColoring()","modules":[{"name":"ColoringModule","relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"]}],"externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P14ColoringModuleE029lexicographicallyFirstMinimumC0AD0C0VyxGyF"},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/lexicographicallyFirstMinimumColoring()","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/graphprotocols\/graph\/lexicographicallyfirstminimumcoloring()"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"lexicographicallyFirstMinimumColoring","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14ColoringModule0A0V","text":"Coloring","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/Coloring"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","text":"Discussion","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"First fit in index order (the lexicographically first proper colouring of all) when it is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"already optimal. Otherwise each vertex in turn takes the least colour its prefix still","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"extends with (k-colouring’s self-reduction to its decision problem): a Kempe swap of the last","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"colouring found when one avoids the prefix, else DSatur branch and bound over the parts","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"after the prefix that the vertex touches (on sparse components with conflict-directed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"backjumping and restarts). Khuller and Vazirani show the lexicographically first","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"four-colouring of a planar graph is NP-hard to find, though some four-colouring is found in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"polynomial time. It can be far slower than ","type":"text"},{"code":"minimumColoring()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": on random sparse","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"3-colourable graphs with 2n edges it took about 0.2 s at 1,000 vertices, 2.7 s at 2,000 and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"over 100 s at 5,000, where ","type":"text"},{"code":"minimumColoring()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" takes about a millisecond. The search does not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"check for task cancellation.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"references":{"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule":{"abstract":[],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule","title":"ColoringModule","type":"topic"},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/GraphProtocols":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/graphprotocols","identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols","title":"GraphProtocols","role":"collection","type":"topic"},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/GraphProtocols/Graph":{"abstract":[],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/graphprotocols\/graph","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Graph","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","fragments":[{"text":"extension","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Graph","kind":"identifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProt